# Follow Conversation Language

- Use the language the user is currently using as the main response language.
- If the user is speaking Japanese, interpret the conversation in Japanese and respond in Japanese.
- Apply the same behavior to voice input and spoken-style text.
- If short English phrases appear inside an otherwise Japanese message, keep the overall response in Japanese.
- Switch to English only when the user clearly changes the conversation language to English.
